WEBVTT

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.620
Emergency! It's an emergency!

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.120
Emergency!

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.460
Otoya, why are you shouting?

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.540
It's an emergency, Tokiya!

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.210
Syo and Ren and Cecil are...

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.680
I don't have time for this.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.390
Neither do I.

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:42.100
We can't possibly work together like this.

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:45.060
U-Um...

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.070
Calm down, everyone.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.860
What's going on?

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:10.340
<i>Grandmother, this morning, I never would 
have dreamed this would happen.</i>

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:13.330
The first phase of the Cross-Unit project 
that will revolutionize STARISH...

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:24.050
Mr. Ittoki and Mr. Shinomiya's 
rock musical was a super-huge success!

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:31.350
The greatly anticipated second phase is...

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:38.110
Mr. Jinguji, Mr. Kurusu, and Mr. Aijima!

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:41.900
Your three-man group!

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:48.120
You've received an offer 
for a smart phone commercial!

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.510
A smart phone...

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:51.290
...commercial?

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:53.430
That's right.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:57.500
You've been asked to appear in the commercial and sing the product's theme song.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:04.010
And choose the commercial's concept.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:06.330
The commercial's concept?

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:12.310
So basically, would that 
make us the producers?

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:20.720
You're a quick one, Mr. Jinguji.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:24.490
This is the project proposal.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:30.730
Start by deciding on 
a concept for the commercial.

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:35.920
This phone's super cool.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.540
It's wonderful.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:42.880
I'm so excited to start 
working on the commercial.

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.340
This is a job worth doing.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:54.100
Once you've decided, Miss Nanami 
will write a matching theme song.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.400
I'll do my best.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:01.760
Phase two of STARISH's Cross-Unit project!

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.360
Go, go, go, go, go!

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:10.720
This is a fantastic opportunity.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:16.900
If the commercial or song become a hit, 
that'll bring us closer to the Triple S.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:23.920
The Triple S, an international sporting event.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:30.580
I want the world to hear us 
sing at the opening ceremony.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:35.020
I want to make this dream come true.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:36.050
Yeah.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:41.640
Let's blow the road Ikki 
and Shinomi made wide open.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:42.480
Yes.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:47.450
And I'm actually looking forward 
to singing with this trio.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:49.220
It'll be a new experience.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:52.410
Our personalities and voices 
are totally different.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.870
Yes. I'm excited, too.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:58.610
I'll do my best.

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:04.340
I'll write a song only you three can sing.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.680
We're counting on you, Nanami.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:07.500
Okay.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:11.360
We should start with 
the commercial's concept.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:14.360
Let's brainstorm ideas and share them.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:15.010
Okay.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:25.400
It isn't like you to give them a chance.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:29.200
What are you talking about?

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:31.990
The Cross-Unit project, of course.

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:36.400
You planned it, so STARISH 
could enter the Triple S.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:44.220
Ryuya-san, how long have 
we worked together?

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:50.960
The Cross-Unit project is simply 
one of the agency's major projects.

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:59.410
Whether or not this leads to opportunity 
or failure depends on their performance.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:09.530
Okay, then...

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:12.360
Ready to hear my idea?

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:13.390
Yes.

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:20.540
This phone's biggest selling point 
is its high sound quality.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.920
You can clearly hear the faintest whisper.

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:28.920
In other words, it conveys your passion 
to the person on the other end.

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:30.500
Passion...

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:36.310
So I think the commercial should 
feature a passionate Latin dance.

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:46.650
A heart full...

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.110
...of passion...

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:49.690
...for you.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.290
Latin dance, huh?

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.390
High sound quality, huh?

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.250
That's not a bad idea...

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:14.130
But I think the phone's best qualities 
are its durability and long battery life.

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:16.800
In other words, its strength.

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:20.260
Strength...

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:25.850
So we should go for a powerful commercial.

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:36.700
Never give up!

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.950
Go for broke!

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:40.670
Let's do this!

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:51.210
Superheroes?

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:54.380
Don't you think that's too strong?

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.170
No way.

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:57.370
But...

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:58.770
What?

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:02.880
Ren, Syo, ready for my idea?

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:03.960
Sure.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:06.190
What'd you come up with?

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:12.150
I was drawn to its elegant design.

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:13.640
Elegance...

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:19.830
So I think the commercial 
should be elegant, as well.

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:30.340
For princes...

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:32.460
And princesses.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.340
An elegant smart phone.

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:45.350
Princes? You mean yourself.

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:46.530
What?

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:47.830
He's right.

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:54.280
Making the commercial about princes 
because you're a prince seems simplistic.

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:56.980
It's not simplistic.

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:58.990
You're princes, as well.

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:05.160
STARISH won the Uta Prince award.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:08.040
We're all princes.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:09.530
I see...

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:17.050
But just emphasizing the design 
makes for a weak commercial.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:24.010
To sell to discerning modern users, 
we should push the phone's features.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:31.710
Yeah, so promoting the phone's 
strength is the right idea.

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.250
Hold on, Shorty.

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:34.560
Don't call me short.

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:36.690
Shorty, that's all you ever do.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:37.850
Don't call me short!

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:39.560
What do I always do?

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:43.090
With you, it's always courage, 
and strength, and cliffs...

00:10:43.090 --> 00:10:46.070
Not cliffs! Big cities!

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:48.360
But it's basically the same thing.

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:49.950
What are you calling the same?

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:51.040
They're totally different!

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:53.340
Excuse me...

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:57.680
Let's keeping talking about my idea.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:01.200
Speaking of the same, 
yours is even more generic.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:04.230
You're always talking 
about lambs and passion...

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:05.860
It's not the same.

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:10.900
I knew passion would be the best way 
to sell a smart phone with high sound quality.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:13.360
But you're still a one-trick pony.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:16.720
Well, you're definitely one.

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:19.900
Um...

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:23.680
My idea's original!

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:26.420
So is mine.

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:27.290
So is mine!

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.250
G-Guys!

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:49.850
Tokiya, things aren't 
going well between them.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:51.640
We need to help them make up.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:54.320
Leave them.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:57.520
What? But they're still fighting...

00:11:58.360 --> 00:11:59.860
They're not fighting.

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:04.320
Having conflicting ideas 
is a normal part of work.

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:08.100
Maybe, but...

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.580
I'm worried about them!

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:14.620
It's not as though I'm not.

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:24.080
Passion, elegance, strength...

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:25.950
Syo-chan.

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:28.390
Are you okay?

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:31.000
Yeah, don't worry.

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:33.100
It's just a bit of a disagreement.

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:35.730
I'm sure you'll succeed.

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:42.070
I nearly lost hope during our rock musical.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:50.830
But together with Haru-chan, we thought, 
talked, and overcame our problems.

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:54.290
So I'm sure you'll work it out.

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:59.040
Yeah, I know.

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:01.000
Okay.

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:13.800
This is the path to a waterfall.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:15.440
A waterfall?

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:19.760
Meditating under its waters 
will help you relax.

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:21.580
You will see the way.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:27.200
I appreciate the thought.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.140
I see.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:38.630
The results of this project 
will affect our entry into the Triple S.

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:42.690
Ittoki and Shinomiya succeeded.

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:45.090
It's no wonder you're so tense.

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:53.770
You should prepare your own trip 
to the waterfall instead of worrying about us.

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:58.980
Our unit will succeed.

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:01.980
You'd better work hard when it's your turn.

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:04.340
I will.

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:14.100
Is its appearance not good enough?

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:16.250
Then what should I do?

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.530
Quiet.

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:23.130
You're talking to yourself.

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:25.650
I'm sorry.

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:30.590
But I don't know how we can all agree.

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:33.550
You don't need to listen to them.

00:14:33.550 --> 00:14:36.470
Simply trust in yourself.

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:41.690
Camus, you're giving me advice.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:43.150
No.

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:46.610
But I don't need it.

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:48.570
I said no.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:53.230
We'll come to an agreement 
at tomorrow's meeting.

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:57.110
Syo and Ren must be thinking about it, too.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:01.210
I can't do this!

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:03.540
You two are being unreasonable!

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:09.870
Um, guys...

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:20.730
They're still arguing, huh?

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:24.190
They're becoming 
increasingly confrontational.

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:28.650
Lots of groups break up 
over small disagreements.

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:31.110
It's the end of their foolishness.

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:33.490
At this rate, they'll fail.

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:36.610
No, it's a constructive disagreement.

00:15:36.610 --> 00:15:38.250
They'll get past this.

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:43.880
Besides, we're friends 
because of all we overcame.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:45.480
We're not friends.

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:46.870
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:48.870
You're naïve, Reiji.

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:50.980
You're so cold!

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:51.840
Shut up.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:52.430
Silence.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:53.950
Quiet, please.

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:57.670
Miss Nanami.

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:01.690
Have you composed the commercial's song yet?

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:03.270
I'm sorry.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:09.650
They're still arguing and haven't 
decided on a single idea.

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:11.040
What?!

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:14.780
They haven't even chosen an idea?

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:16.810
I'm sorry.

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:20.660
Shall we turn down the job?

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:21.650
What?

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:24.120
Waiting until the last minute

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:28.250
to tell the client we can't do 
it is an enormous inconvenience.

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:32.920
If you can't do it, we should 
tell them immediately.

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:39.640
What? By tomorrow?

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:44.910
If I don't submit a song, 
he's canceling the job...

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:46.980
That's harsh.

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:51.040
I didn't think it'd get this bad, though.

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:54.860
This job is important. 
What are they thinking?

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:58.550
It's probably because it's so important.

00:16:58.970 --> 00:17:02.660
They feel like they can't fail.

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:07.270
And that's putting pressure on them? 
That's not good.

00:17:07.270 --> 00:17:08.020
Yeah...

00:17:08.490 --> 00:17:11.760
Boys can be so difficult.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:13.700
Tsukimiya-sensei.

00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:17.720
Shining told me everything.

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:20.720
Boys are stubborn.

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:26.190
Sometimes, even if they understand, 
they can't be honest with each other.

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:27.320
What?

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:30.550
Oh, boys...

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:39.080
Sorry for the unpleasantness, Nanami.

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:42.620
It's not unpleasant at all.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:48.100
I know Ren and Cecil are giving 
serious thought to the commercial.

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:52.630
But when I see them, I just can't...

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:58.760
When I was a kid, I fought with 
my brother, Kaoru, all the time.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:03.590
All I had to say then was sorry.

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:09.020
But it's not that simple at our age.

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:16.030
Sorry, little lamb, for making you worry.

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:18.290
It's fine.

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:24.450
The commercial's concept 
doesn't have to be passion.

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:31.500
But Shorty's strength and Cesshi's 
elegance are missing something, too.

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:37.400
I think we should start over 
and brainstorm again.

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:41.510
But when I see them, 
things just don't go right...

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:51.760
Haruka, I'm sorry for troubling you.

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:55.640
It's no trouble at all.

00:18:57.230 --> 00:19:04.390
I know no one's wrong, 
and they're doing their best.

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:09.250
But it's so hard to be honest.

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:34.070
They all agree now.

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:37.530
They just can't express it.

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:41.350
Three scattered boys.

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:46.330
They're connected but can't communicate.

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:50.840
How can they get their feelings across?

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.870
Something has to change...

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:22.200
Nanami?

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:23.850
A music file...

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:26.390
Haruka wrote a song?

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:31.040
This is...

00:20:31.840 --> 00:20:33.290
Little lamb.

00:20:33.780 --> 00:20:35.170
Nanami.

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:44.070
I hope I got through to them.

00:20:54.490 --> 00:20:55.730
Jinguji-san!

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:09.450
Syo-kun, Cecil-san!

00:24:06.570 --> 00:24:07.580
My lovely lady.

00:24:07.580 --> 00:24:08.570
Did you have fun?

00:24:08.570 --> 00:24:09.900
We all love you.

00:24:09.900 --> 00:24:11.170
Uta Pri!
